          "distinct": false,
          "id": "d3a06831ec3cb59d0dda9a75a410bef1375ebf54",
          "message": "docs(research): engine performance review — runtime/build/coverage levers from the 2026-07 profiling digests [FABLE-5] (#1397)\n\n* docs(research): engine performance review — runtime/build/coverage levers from the 2026-07 profiling digests [FABLE-5]\n\nDesign record over the two Opus profiling digests (runtime hot-path perf capture +\ncold-build --timings profile). Five un-beaded runtime levers extending sq-7d3dj\n(radix-sorted permutation indexes, prefix-memoized IRI validation, hash-join\nsingle-hash + batch emission as the M4 contract, LFTJ small-arity specialization,\nutf8_unchecked with unsafe-register discipline), four source-level build levers\ndisjoint from sq-6vshe's CI-side program (engine test-crate consolidation,\nship-vs-release-fast profile split, monomorphization diet feeding the split RFC,\ndev-dep trim), and two coverage-lane levers beyond the shard work (changed-cone\ncoverage with baseline inheritance, instrumentation-weight diet with governed\nre-baseline). All figures relative/non-canonical; adoption proves on EC2 + ratchets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(research): fill in the created bead IDs (sq-7d3dj.17-.21, sq-6vshe.8-.13) [FABLE-5]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T02:42:37Z",
