          "distinct": false,
          "id": "45ecda526b1f349b112dc0ba2c5b6351643acbde",
          "message": "test(sparq-mpc): mutation-directed Shamir/robust unit tests + floor 88->90 (sq-qcnn.26) [OPUS-4.8] (#1403)\n\n* test(sparq-mpc): mutation-directed direct unit tests on Shamir/robust algebra + raise coverage floor 88->90 (sq-qcnn.26) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nTest-only on a security crate: NO MPC primitive logic changed (the src diff is\npure +insertions inside #[cfg(test)] modules), semi-honest scope, NO\nsoundness/security claim (sq-qhy4 gates that).\n\nEnumerated survivors with `cargo mutants -p sparq-mpc -f shamir.rs -f robust.rs`\n(260 mutants; 18 missed by the prior suite) and added 19 DIRECT, value-asserting\nunit tests that kill 10 of them across the comparison-flip / numeric-arithmetic /\n&&-||-guard-flip / default-body classes the end-to-end round-trips missed:\n\n- robust.rs Berlekamp-Welch helpers: eval_poly, trim_trailing_zeros,\n  poly_mul_linear, poly_divmod (exact / nonzero-rem / low-degree / zero-divisor),\n  lagrange_at_zero(_poly), solve_linear_system, for_each_combination,\n  check_distinct_points, disagreeing_points, berlekamp_welch.\n- shamir.rs: degree_reduce fail-closed precondition (deficient n<2t+1 via\n  with_unchecked_threshold), the degree-2t equality-open per-operator security\n  boundary + the malicious_security no-redundancy (n<=t+1) arm, dealer\n  parties/threshold accessors, ShamirDealer/MacSession Debug redaction, and\n  extract_single_integer shape guards.\n\n18 survivors before -> 8 after. The 8 remaining are PROVABLY-EQUIVALENT\n(documented in bench/coverage-floor.json, not gamed) across 5 classes: the\nunreachable n==degree branch; the never-usable e_max budget enlargements (masked\nby berlekamp_welch's own n<degree+2e+1 None-return); the berlekamp rem-exactness\ncheck masked by the downstream disagreeing_points re-verification; the\nbest_effort_suspects tie-break (unobservable in the guaranteed regime); and the\nnon-observable MacSession Drop alpha-zeroize.\n\nMeasured line% 94.42 (default features, cargo llvm-cov -p sparq-mpc); floor 88->90.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(mpc): assert cleartext α value is ABSENT from MacSession Debug (sq-qcnn.26) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nCopilot review: `mac_session_debug_labels_struct_and_redacts_alpha` asserted a\nredaction LABEL was present but never asserted the cleartext session MAC key α\nvalue was absent — a future Debug that printed α alongside the label would still\npass. Capture `session.alpha_for_test()`'s Debug rendering and assert it is NOT a\nsubstring of `format!(\"{session:?}\")`, pinning the actual redaction property.\nTests-only; no MPC-logic change, no soundness claim (sq-qhy4).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
